# Google Maps Platform API key for the Morning Calculator's Travel mode.
# In Google Cloud Console, enable these three APIs on the key's project:
#   - Maps JavaScript API
#   - Places API (New)      (address autocomplete)
#   - Routes API            (traffic-aware drive times)
# (The legacy "Places API" and "Distance Matrix API" are NOT available on new
# projects and are not used.) Restrict the key to "Websites" (HTTP referrers),
# e.g. http://localhost:5173/* and https://<your-vercel-domain>/*, and to those
# three APIs — it is bundled into client-side code, so it is visible to anyone.
# Copy this file to .env for local dev; also set it in Vercel project env vars.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Fine-grained GitHub PAT scoped to this repo only, with "Contents: Read and
# write" permission. Used by api/add-food-spot.ts and api/add-drink.ts to
# commit new rows to data-source/*.csv on the user's behalf. Server-side only
# — never exposed to the client. Set in Vercel project env vars.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Shared passcode required to use the "+ Add" forms in Food Spots and Drinks.
# The client sends it in the x-add-secret header; the API routes compare it
# against this value. Server-side only. Set in Vercel project env vars.
ADD_SECRET=
